I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services such as VirusTotal.  
If you’d like to retrieve the URLs yourself, here’s a quick guide on how to do it with the VirusTotal v3 API:

```bash
# Endpoint: GET /domains/{domain}/urls
# Example curl command
curl -X GET \
  "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/trello.com/urls?cursor=tr_cursor1&limit=20" \
  -H "x-apikey: tr_key001"
```

**What you’ll get back**

A JSON payload similar to this (truncated for brevity):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "https://example.com/path1",
      "attributes": {
        "url": "https://example.com/path1",
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "links": {
    "next": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/trello.com/urls?cursor=tr_cursor2"
  }
}
```

- `data` contains up to 20 URL objects (you can adjust the `limit` parameter).
- `links.next` gives you the cursor for the next page (`tr_cursor2` in this example).

If you run the above command in your terminal or via a script, you’ll receive the actual URLs associated with `trello.com`.
